---
Title: Marry Me Chicken
Servings: 2-3 people
Tags: Nom Nom Central, Chicken, Italian-American, 
Link: https://gypsyplate.com/marry-me-chicken/
---

Mix all the chicken seasoning ingredinets in a #small bowl{}:  @Paprika{1}, @Parsley{1 tsp}
@Salt{1/2 tsp}
@Pepper{1/2 tsp}

Season the @Chicken Thighs or Breasts{5-6 pieces} on both sides. 

Dredge the chicken in @Flour{1/4 cup} and shake off any excess.

In a #large skillet{}, melt the @Butter{2 Tablespoons} on medium heat. 

Brown the chicken, skin side first for ~{6-7 minutes} on each side, or until golden brown. Transfer onto a #plate and set aside.

In the same pan, add a little more butter if needed and sauté chopped @Shallot{1} for a minute. 

Add @Garlic{4 cloves} and cook for  ~{1 minute}, or until it's fragrant. 

Add @Red Chili Flakes{1 teaspoon}, @Thyme{1 teaspoon} and @Oregano{1 teaspoon} and mix well. 

Add in chopped @Sun Dried Tomatoes{1/3 cup} and cook for ~{2-3 minutes}.

Adjust the heat to medium-low, and add the @Heavy Cream{1 cup}, @Chicken Stock{1/2 cup} and the @Parmesan Cheese{3/4 cup} to the skillet. Mix and stir well till the cheese melts, and simmer it for ~{4-5 minutes}.

Mix in @Basil Leaves{1/4 cup} and place the chicken thighs in skin side up. Adjust the heat to medium low, cover, and cook till chicken is cooked through, stirring the sauce occasionally. Internal temperature for chicken thighs reaches 80-190°F and chicken breast cook till internal temperature reaches 165°F.

Garnish with some more basil leaves and serve immediately. 